      "record_ids": ["persons:QQ102701B", "PEN-00072", "CAP-00067", "TEN-4169"],
      "reason": "Dilys Roberts (born 1951-11-21) lives in Wales and is over State Pension age (PC-1). She is single with no partner (PC-2 not applicable). Savings are £8,239, below the £10,000 threshold, so no notional income from savings (PC-3). Her actual weekly income is £281.10 (state pension £242.66 + private pension £38.44). The Guarantee Credit threshold for a single person is £238 (PC-4). Assessed income (£281.10) exceeds the threshold, so she is not entitled to Guarantee Credit (PC-5)."
    },
    {
      "benefit": "attendance_allowance",
      "decision": "not_eligible",
      "weekly_amount": 0,
      "clause_ids": ["AA-1", "AA-2", "AA-3", "AA-4", "AA-5", "AA-6"],
      "record_ids": ["persons:QQ102701B", "note:HH-070.txt"],
      "reason": "Dilys has reached State Pension age and has been resident in Great Britain since 1975 (AA-1, AA-4). However, the caseworker note states she 'manages personal care independently and did not report any difficulties', indicating she does not need help with personal care or supervision (AA-2). There is no evidence she has needed such help for at least 6 months (AA-3). She does not receive DLA, PIP or Adult Disability Payment (AA-5). Therefore she does not meet the disability criteria for Attendance Allowance."
    },
    {
      "benefit": "council_tax_reduction",
      "decision": "eligible",
      "weekly_amount": 20.96,
      "clause_ids": ["CTR-1", "CTR-2", "CTR-3", "CTR-5", "CTR-6"],
      "record_ids": ["persons:QQ102701B", "CT-70897", "PEN-00072", "CAP-00067"],
      "reason": "Dilys is over State Pension age (CTR-2) and is the liable council tax payer for her home in Wales (CTR-3). She does not receive Guarantee Credit (CTR-4 not met). Capital is £8,239, below the £16,000 limit (CTR-5). Using the pensioner scheme: applicable amount = £238 (single). Weekly income = £281.10, savings below £10,000 so no notional income. Income above applicable = £43.10. 20% taper = £8.62. Net annual council tax charge after 25% single person discount = £2,051.16 × 0.75 = £1,538.37; weekly net charge = £29.58. Weekly reduction = £29.58 − £8.62 = £20.96 > 0, so she is eligible for a reduction of £20.96 per week (CTR-6)."
    },
    {
      "benefit": "warm_home_discount",
      "decision": "not_eligible",
      "weekly_amount": 0,
      "clause_ids": ["WHD-1", "WHD-2", "WHD-3"],
      "record_ids": ["persons:QQ102701B", "TEN-4169", "PEN-00072", "note:HH-070.txt"],
      "reason": "The scheme covers Wales (WHD-1) and Dilys's name is on the electricity bill (WHD-3). However, eligibility requires that on 23 August 2026 she or her partner received a qualifying means-tested benefit (Pension Credit, Housing Benefit, Universal Credit, or income-related ESA) (WHD-2). She is not entitled to Pension Credit (see pension_credit decision), and there is no record of her receiving any of the other qualifying benefits. Therefore she does not meet the benefit condition."
    }
  ]
